# Negative case 2: the torn-write fallback.
# vendor/streamdb-v3/negative/corpus.header-flip.streamdb is corpus.streamdb
# with the byte at file offset 136 XORed with 0xFF -- the low byte of header
# slot 1's commit-sequence field. Slot 1 holds seq=3, the newest commit, all
# 24 documents; slot 0 holds seq=2, the 20 documents of this corpus's first
# `streamdb_flush()`. The flip breaks slot 1's own trailing CRC, so that slot
# no longer validates and the newest slot that DOES is slot 0.
#
# What expectation.json records the reference reader doing: open and probe
# succeed, against the older commit; "documents: 20, trie nodes: 316"; the 20
# documents of that commit read back byte-exact; models/asset_020.t3dm,
# sprites/asset_021.sprite, sfx/asset_022.wav64 and music/asset_023.xm64 each
# return STREAMDB_EMB_ERR_NOT_FOUND; "suffix '.t3dm' -> 4 match(es)".
#
# expected.out (25,099 bytes) is all of that, byte by byte: section 0 carries
# sequence 2, section 1 carries 20 documents / 316 trie nodes / winning slot
# 0, the last four keys carry verdict 1 (not found) with no payload, and the
# `.t3dm` count is 4 rather than 5 with models/asset_020.t3dm's row gone from
# the traversal order and the other four unmoved.
#
# THIS IS THE CASE THE WHOLE TWO-SLOT HEADER EXISTS FOR, and it is only
# available because the corpus was packed with two `streamdb_flush()` calls
# (PROVENANCE.md, `pack2.c`): a single-flush container has one slot that ever
# validates, so corrupting it fails the open instead of demonstrating the
# fallback.
TEST: expect-exit=0 stdin=vendor/streamdb-v3/negative/corpus.header-flip.streamdb sources=examples/streamdb/lector_streamdb.exsc,examples/streamdb/probatio.exsc cross=yes
